Subject: [PATCH] mtk: lpm: schedule failed retention probes from current time

The retention readiness probe is a retry, not a periodic accounting deadline.
Rearming by adding the interval to the old expiry can leave it in the past
after a delayed callback, causing immediate catch-up probes until it catches
up with jiffies. Schedule the next attempt from the current jiffies instead.

Keep the per-CPU target, firmware readiness test, device-tree interval and
successful-probe termination unchanged. Do not make this timer deferrable:
that could postpone enabling CPU retention on an otherwise idle CPU.

This targets the published MTK_kernel_device_modules platform/v2 source.
It is an UNAPPLIED vendor candidate, not active in the common EVONIX kernel.
Confirm the deployed platform version and hotplug/suspend behavior before
building or packaging its module.

diff --git a/drivers/misc/mediatek/lpm/modules/platform/v2/lpm_plat_apmcu.c b/drivers/misc/mediatek/lpm/modules/platform/v2/lpm_plat_apmcu.c
--- a/drivers/misc/mediatek/lpm/modules/platform/v2/lpm_plat_apmcu.c
+++ b/drivers/misc/mediatek/lpm/modules/platform/v2/lpm_plat_apmcu.c
@@ -192,7 +192,7 @@
 	unsigned int cur_cpu = smp_processor_id();
 
 	if (cur_cpu != crtd->cpu) {
-		crtd->ret_timer.expires += ((unsigned long)cpu_ret_check_interval);
+		crtd->ret_timer.expires = jiffies + cpu_ret_check_interval;
 		add_timer_on(&crtd->ret_timer, crtd->cpu);
 		return;
 	}
@@ -203,7 +203,7 @@
 		crtd->ret_ready = 1;
 		del_timer(&crtd->ret_timer);
 	} else if (!timer_pending(&crtd->ret_timer)) {
-		crtd->ret_timer.expires += ((unsigned long)cpu_ret_check_interval);
+		crtd->ret_timer.expires = jiffies + cpu_ret_check_interval;
 		add_timer_on(&crtd->ret_timer, cur_cpu);
 	}
 	pr_info("[name:cpu_pm&] cpu_ret_check\n");
